    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hebron grew near the old Bridges Settlement of 1843, twenty‑one miles southeast of Denton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.allacrosstexas.com/texas-ghost-town.php?city=Hebron"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its historic center sits where two railroads once met, near present‑day East Hebron Parkway and 1st Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebron%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town incorporated in 1961 to stop neighboring Plano and Carrollton from annexing its land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
